## BUSINESS ANALYSIS (2026-06-13) — BA lens
Deep BA review + implemented artifacts. Full report: docs/BUSINESS_ANALYSIS.md
(git-tracked). Findings BA1–BA8; the report's risk register (R1–R8) and MoSCoW
roadmap re-frame the engineering backlog (D5/G1–G17/DX) by adoption impact.

- [x] **BA-DOCS** — DONE 2026-06-13: created docs/BUSINESS_ANALYSIS.md (vision,
      P1–P4 personas + ICP, quantified value hypotheses, competitive/SWOT,
      stakeholder map, FR/NFR, KPIs, MoSCoW roadmap, risk register, adoption
      funnel + enterprise-readiness gate, validation plan); SECURITY.md
      (disclosure + data-handling); .github issue/feature templates + support
      config (feedback loop); README trademark disclaimer + compatibility/auth
      notes + doc links.
- [ ] **BA1. No target persona / user-research loop** — roadmap is self-derived.
      ACTION (owner): run 5–8 interviews (SI/consultancy beachhead); tie roadmap
      to demand. Feedback loop now opened via issue templates.
- [ ] **BA2. Value proposition not quantified** — hypotheses in §3 need baseline
      + after measurement with 1–2 pilot teams.
- [x] **BA3. Competitive one-pager** — DONE 2026-06-14: docs/COMPARISON.md —
      Syncrona vs ServiceNow native Git, Sincronia, and update sets (capability
      matrix, when-to-choose, the one-line difference, honest gaps). Linked from
      README and BUSINESS_ANALYSIS §4.
- [~] **BA4. Enterprise auth (Basic only)** is the #1 paying-market blocker —
      promote G1 (OAuth/SSO) to "Must". (Tech work tracked as G1.) MOSTLY DONE:
      the premise no longer holds — G1 landed 2026-06-16, so auth is not
      Basic-only. `syncrona login` offers Basic, OAuth (password,
      client-credentials, JWT-bearer) and an inbound REST API key, each with
      optional mutual TLS. REMAINING [owner decision]: the interactive
      authorization-code / true-SSO grant, which needs a redirect URI and a
      registered OAuth app — a product decision, not engineering work
      (`ROADMAP.md:272`).
- [ ] **BA5. No business model / sustainability / bus factor 1** — decide
      OSS-only vs OSS+paid-support; document ownership; recruit co-maintainer.
- [ ] **BA6. Brand fragmentation** (syncrona / SyncroNow AI / syncrona /
      @syncrona) — unify on one name across npm/repo/CLI [owner decision].
- [ ] **BA7. No success metrics / KPIs** — instrument once opt-in telemetry (G7)
      lands; KPI set defined in §7.
- [~] **BA8. Provenance / IP (Risk R1)** — LICENSING FIX APPLIED 2026-06-21.
      Deep BA found the real conflict: upstream Sincronia is **GPL-3.0**
      (LICENSE file + @sincronia/core package.json) but this fork was relicensed
      to **MIT** with no attribution — a GPL violation that blocked any
      distribution. Fixed: LICENSE replaced with verbatim GPL-3.0, all 14
      package.json `license` fields → `GPL-3.0-or-later`, added `NOTICE`
      (copyright + Sincronia/Nuvolo attribution + trademark notice), README
      license section rewritten. Gate green. REMAINING [owner/legal]: a lawyer's
      sign-off on the GPL-3.0-only vs -or-later variant and that no
      employer-proprietary code is mixed in, BEFORE the first public publish.
      Note: GPL copyleft forecloses a closed-source/proprietary paid tier
      (see deep BA §1/§3 — OSS or SaaS/support monetization only).
